  <prompt>Build the P&amp;P document architecture on sprk_document (NO new sprk_policy entity): add a sprk_documentcategory optionset discriminator (Operational/Policy/Reference-Golden — do NOT overload the AI-populated sprk_documenttype) + governance fields (status/effective/expiration) on sprk_document; wire category→index routing through the existing multi-index, per-record-routable lifecycle (sprk_ai_search_index lookup + SearchIndexNameResolver + allow-list); author a Policy Library sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy) read via BffDataverseClient; and add governance-state index-trim fields (status/effective/published) + a query-time filter so retrieval never surfaces an unpublished/expired policy. Design the mechanism GENERAL (Reference-Golden reuses it via sprk_analysisknowledge→ReferenceIndexingService→spaarke-rag-references) but BUILD only Policy in R2 (FR-25).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Dataverse schema (dataverse-create-schema — Web API + PowerShell); AI-Search index lifecycle (multi-index, per-record-routable); the DataGrid framework (sprk_gridconfiguration + BffDataverseClient); ASP.NET Minimal API (ADR-008/019) for any BFF index-routing/query change.</role>
  <goal>sprk_document carries a sprk_documentcategory optionset (Operational/Policy/Reference-Golden) + governance fields (status/effective/expiration); a Policy-category document is (re)indexed to a policy AI-Search index via the existing category→index routing (SearchIndexNameResolver + sprk_ai_search_index + allow-list); the policy index schema carries governance-trim fields (status/effective/published) with a query-time filter so unpublished/expired/restricted policies never surface; a Policy Library sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy) exists and reads read-only via BffDataverseClient. The routing + trim mechanism is authored generally (Reference-Golden documented as reusing it) but only Policy is built + wired in R2.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-25 (spec.md line 257): P&amp;P library reuses sprk_document (NOT a new sprk_policy entity — eliminated 2026-08-06 per grounding) + a new sprk_documentcategory discriminator (Operational/Policy/Reference-Golden; do NOT overload the single-valued AI-populated sprk_documenttype) + governance fields (status/effective/expiration) + SPE storage + the existing document→AI-Search indexing lifecycle, which is already multi-index + per-record-routable (sprk_ai_search_index lookup + SearchIndexNameResolver + allow-list, shipped by multi-container-multi-index-r1) — so routing Policy docs to a policy index is a small category→index wire-up, not new plumbing. Golden/Reference RAG docs reuse the SAME mechanism (category=Reference-Golden → sprk_analysisknowledge delivery=RagIndex → ReferenceIndexingService → spaarke-rag-references). Two read roles kept separate: (a) grounding — Ask Legal policy_search (FR-26/051) hits the AI-Search policy index; (b) browse — the Policy Library grid reads sprk_document via sprk_gridconfiguration + BffDataverseClient. GENUINELY NEW: governance-state trim fields (status/effective/published) are not on any index schema today → add index fields + a query-time filter (§12 C folds this into the P5 assistant spike's trim item; build the schema + trim here). §12(C): a general "typed document → typed RAG index → typed grid" capability, not a policy one-off. Authoring is by the law department as core users in the MDA (external portal is read-only on P&amp;P) — reuse the existing document upload wizard + SPE + the sprk_document-search-index-lifecycle; do NOT build new authoring plumbing.</background>
