  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the deployed schema, when a sprk_document is set to category=Policy with governance fields (status/effective/expiration), then all persist and category is a distinct field from the AI-populated sprk_documenttype (not overloaded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Published policy document, when the indexing lifecycle runs, then it is routed to the policy AI-Search index via SearchIndexNameResolver + the allow-list (category→index) with no new pipeline.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (governance trim): given an unpublished or expired policy, when retrieval queries the policy index, then the query-time filter excludes it — it never surfaces (verified by a negative test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Policy Library grid, when it loads, then it reads sprk_document via a sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy) through BffDataverseClient read-only — no hand-rolled grid in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the routing + trim mechanism, when reviewed, then it is authored generally (Reference-Golden documented as reusing sprk_analysisknowledge→ReferenceIndexingService→spaarke-rag-references) but only Policy is built + wired in R2 (no Reference indexing in the diff).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no sprk_policy entity is created — the diff extends sprk_document only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the BFF build, when dotnet publish -c Release runs, then compressed size is reported with delta vs 46.90 MB and is ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
    <existing>sprk_document + sprk_documenttype (AI-populated picklist) exist; the indexing lifecycle is already multi-index + per-record-routable (RagIndexingJobHandler:115-165 + SearchIndexNameResolver + sprk_ai_search_index allow-list, shipped by multi-container-multi-index-r1); the DataGrid framework + BffDataverseClient exist. What does NOT exist: a category discriminator, governance fields, governance-state index trim (KnowledgeDocument has only tenantId + privilege_group_ids today — no status/effective), and a Policy Library grid config.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend sprk_document (additive optionset + governance fields), extend the existing routing (add a category branch), extend the index schema (governance-trim fields), and author a grid CONFIG record (not new grid code). No new entity, no new pipeline, no new grid component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the category discriminator + governance fields + trim, there is no way to store, route, or safely surface policies: FR-25's browse library has no filtered data source, and FR-26/051's policy_search would ground on unpublished/expired content (a data-leakage/compliance failure). Overloading sprk_documenttype would collide with the AI-populated type and break classification.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <notes>Spec FR-25 (line 257) + §12(C). NO sprk_policy entity. Category discriminator separate from AI-populated sprk_documenttype. Governance-state trim (status/effective/published) is the one genuinely-new plumbing piece — build the fields + query filter here; the P5 spike (050) refines its security requirements for the assistant. Design general (typed doc → typed index → typed grid) but build only Policy. §10 BFF: Placement Justification + publish size + conflict-check mandatory. Authoring is by law-dept core users in the MDA (external portal read-only) — reuse the existing upload wizard + lifecycle, no new authoring plumbing.</notes>
